flowmux is an unofficial Linux/GTK4 reimplementation inspired by cmux
(https://github.com/manaflow-ai/cmux), a macOS/AppKit terminal for AI
coding agents. The cmux repository's default license is
GPL-3.0-or-later. Its LICENSE also states that separate commercial terms
may be offered for material for which Manaflow controls the necessary
rights. flowmux uses no commercial license and is distributed only under
GPL-3.0-or-later.

Because cmux is available under GPL-3.0-or-later, the upstream copyright
notice is preserved:

    Copyright (c) 2024-present Manaflow, Inc.

flowmux does not redistribute cmux source code; it independently
reimplements observable behavior described in cmux's public
documentation (README, cmux.com/docs, CHANGELOG, configuration schemas)
for Linux desktop environments.

Trademarks
----------

"cmux" and "Manaflow" are not used as project, package, binary, or
distribution names by flowmux. The "flowmux" name is intentionally distinct.
References to cmux in documentation are for attribution and behavioral
reference only.

Third-party components
----------------------

Runtime dependencies retain their own licenses; see
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the dependency license inventory generated
from Cargo metadata.

Built-in theme colors, the default terminal palette, and Markdown
specification fixtures retain their own licenses and attribution; see
THIRD_PARTY_ASSET_NOTICES.md.

The image viewer links the system ThorVG library (MIT), which is
installed separately (see scripts/install-thorvg.sh) and, like GTK,
libadwaita, and WebKitGTK, retains its own distribution license.
